# T0072 — Project Overview / Document full display

## Goal

Project Overview description and Project Documents should show their full Markdown content without a fixed-height resizable editor box. The page (or viewport) scrolls when content is longer than the screen; no drag-resize handle on these surfaces.

## Decisions (from interview)

1. **Scope:** Overview + Documents only. Leave Ideas, Wiki, Task notes, boards, etc. on the existing fixed/resizable height behavior.
2. **Modes:** Apply to both edit and read-only/preview for these surfaces.
3. **Resize handle:** Remove on these surfaces. Vertical scrolling (page/viewport) is the overflow mechanism when needed.
4. **Focus / Expand:** Kept (approved with defaults). Fullscreen Focus still available on Overview/Documents; in Focus mode the editor uses an inner scrollbar.

## Approach

1. Add an `autoHeight` prop (name flexible) on shared `MarkdownEditor`:
   - No fixed `height` on the surface; height follows content.
   - Hide/disable the vertical resize handle and related drag/clamp logic for that instance.
   - Surface overflow visible / not an inner scroll trap so the document page scrolls naturally when content exceeds the viewport.
   - Sensible minimum height for empty editors so empty Overview/Documents still look usable.
2. Wire `autoHeight` on `ProjectDetailPage`:
   - Overview description (edit + `readOnly`).
   - Document body editor.
3. CSS: support class (e.g. `.md-editor--auto-height`) so surface/prose min-height and overflow behave correctly without breaking `fill` / fixed-height callers.
4. Do **not** change other `MarkdownEditor` call sites.

## Out of scope

- Ideas, Wiki, TaskBoard notes, Kanban, TodoList, TaskHistory editors.
- Changing Focus mode behavior unless requested at approval.
- Schema / API changes.

## QA follow-ups

- Removed the bordered/rounded “box” chrome around Overview and Document `autoHeight` markdown (content sits flush; Focus mode still uses the framed fullscreen overlay). Toolbar keeps a light bordered bar when editing outside Focus.
- Restored the outline/rounded box **only while actively editing** (`md-editor--editing`). Preview/read-only stays flush. Wiki view (not page-edit) uses `autoHeight` + readonly unframed styles so Documents/Wiki have no border when not editing.

